IN THE HIGH COURT OF DELHI
CASE NO: W.P. (Crl.) No. 135 of 2008
CITATION: 2008 (105) DRJ 721
YEAR: 2008

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: S. Ravindra Bhat

PARTIES:
Avnish Bajaj (Bazee.com) vs State

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Information Technology Act, 2000, Indian Penal Code, 1860

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 67 IT Act, Section 79 IT Act, Section 292 IPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
intermediary liability, safe harbor, obscene content, director liability

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Addressed intermediary liability for user-generated content hosted on an e-commerce platform, prompting the subsequent amendment of Section 79 to introduce the safe harbor doctrine.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 67 IT Act, Section 79 IT Act, Section 292 IPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

